### 🔴 CRITICAL STOP #1: `FixyachipsMasterRole` — Replace + Delete

```
Logical ID:        FixyachipsMasterRole
Action:            Modify
Replacement:       TRUE
Policy Action:     ReplaceAndDelete
```

**What this means in plain English:**

```
CloudFormation will:

  1. Create a brand new IAM Role with a new name
  2. Delete the OLD IAM Role
  3. Lambda still points to the OLD role ARN during the gap
  4. All Lambda invocations FAIL with AccessDeniedException
  5. Every signup attempt returns 500 error
  6. Every user who tries to sign up gets an error

The gap between delete-old and attach-new
can be 30 seconds to 3 minutes.
During a deploy that is unacceptable.
```

**Why is it replacing instead of modifying?**

```yaml
# YOU ADDED THIS LINE — this is the trigger
RoleName: !Sub 'FixyachipsMasterRole-${AWS::StackName}'

# The LIVE template has NO RoleName property
# CloudFormation auto-generated a name like:
# fixyachips-stack-FixyachipsMasterRole-XKCD1234

# When you add an explicit RoleName to an existing role
# CloudFormation MUST replace it — names are immutable
# Replace = Delete old + Create new = downtime window
```

**Fix — two options:**

```yaml
# OPTION A (Recommended for zero downtime):
# Remove the RoleName property entirely
# Let CloudFormation keep the auto-generated name
# Modify will change to False — no replacement

FixyachipsMasterRole:
  Type: 'AWS::IAM::Role'
  Properties:
    # DELETE THIS LINE:
    # RoleName: !Sub 'FixyachipsMasterRole-${AWS::StackName}'
    Description: 'Lambda execution role — scoped to S3, DynamoDB, SES only'
    AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
      ...


# OPTION B (If you need the explicit name):
# Deploy at low-traffic time (2-3am)
# The replacement window is ~60-90 seconds
# Acceptable if you have zero users right now
```

